⸻

20. Definition of Done

Phase 19 is complete when:

1. The application defaults to local-only processing.
2. Remote endpoints cannot be silently used.
3. Screenshots are not persistently stored during normal operation.
4. OCR/translation processing uses ephemeral visual data wherever practical.
5. Session recording is explicitly opt-in.
6. Users can immediately stop translation/capture.
7. Translation queues discard stale work instead of accumulating indefinitely.
8. No DRM/access-control circumvention exists.
9. No presentation redistribution functionality exists.
10. Documentation accurately describes the application as a real-time local translation/accessibility layer.
11. Documentation does not make unsupported claims of legal or company-policy compliance.
12. Automated tests cover the privacy and retention requirements.

⸻

Final Principle

The application should follow this principle:

See it → understand it → translate it → discard the unnecessary source data.

The objective is not to own, archive, reproduce, or redistribute the presentation.

The objective is to make foreign-language content that the user is already viewing understandable in real time.